<title>UK: Reed pares gains on firm's stg concerns.</title>
<headline>Reed pares gains on firm's stg concerns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Reed International Plc pared early gains on Wednesday after the company warned of the repercussions of the sterling's strength.</p>
<p>The currency's appreciation will have a &quot;marked&quot; effect on its profits during the first half, Ian Irvine said in his AGM statement.</p>
<p>At 1111 GMT, the stock was trading at 1100-1/2p, up 7p from Tuesday's close but down from 1112p reached before the statement was released.</p>
</text>
